unexpected situations. This is achieved by incorporating semantic attention maps and unsupervised 'attention' updates into the metareasoning processes. To accommodate environmental dynamics, 'lines of thought' are used to bridge context-specific objects with abstracted attentions, while meta-information is monitored and controlled at the meta-level for effective reasoning. The practicality of the proposed approach is demonstrated through cloud robots deployed in real-world scenarios, showing improved performance and robustness."}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/W4414077155", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009522472.003", "title": "Metacognitive AI", "publication_year": 2025, "type": "book-chapter", "cited_by_count": 0, "open_access": {"is_oa": true, "oa_status": "bronze", "oa_url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/00EEF41B191FD22C5D743E60C7DE0DEE/9781009522458c1_3-22.pdf/metacognitive-ai.pdf", "any_repository_has_fulltext": false}, "primary_location": {"id": "doi:10.1017/9781009522472.003", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009522472.003", "is_oa": true, "landing_page_url": "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009522472.003", "pdf_url": "https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/00EEF41B191FD22C5D743E60C7DE0DEE/9781009522458c1_3-22.pdf/metacognitive-ai.pdf", "source": {"id": "https://openalex.org/S4306462995", "display_name": "Cambridge University Press eBooks", "issn_l": null, "issn": null, "is_oa": false, "is_in_doaj": false, "is_core": false, "listed_in": [], "host_organization": "https://openalex.org/P4310311721", "host_organization_name": "Cambridge University Press", "host_organization_lineage": ["https://openalex.org/P4310311721", "https://openalex.org/P4310311702"], "host_organization_lineage_names": ["Cambridge University Press", "University of Cambridge"], "type": "ebook platform"}, "license": null, "license_id": null, "version": "publishedVersion", "is_accepted": true, "is_published": true